/*#############################################################################################
# ---- PosColMapCombinatorForPerspectiveFusion ----
# Project: IthacaEmetteurRecepteur by FrenchTouchFactory
# Resp. : François
# Author(s): François Bouille (f.bouille@frenchtouchfactory.com)
# Starting date : 2024/04/04
# Latest version date : created on 2024/12/09
# Problem : Isometric or orthogonal fusion induces a displaying issue with a perspective camera. The perspective sees unwanted datas and hide datas generated by the isometric fusion. 
# Hypothesis : Cubic ortho fusion is usefull to store fused data and export it with a good resolution, but is not perfect for display as exposed. Developping a perspective fusion can solve this issue.  
# Description: V1.0 : Solves the perspective problem when displaying a projected planar mesh. From several Tuple Position & Color we project each point of the point cloud on the front face of a cube following the orientation of the main camera. The point on this plane is defined by the intersection of
# the line (point-camera position) and the plane. The datas are fused like we already did in the ortho fusion. To compensate the density issues appearing when the camera get closer to the character
# we apply a damping function and reduce the size of the cube (consequently the plane), we also added the option not to fuse the cameras located at more than 90° from the display camera for optimisation purposes.
# In the compute shader the comparator was modified from != 0 to >0.01 brcause from some reason the very small values are interpreted as 0 values.
# We added a "fusion" boolean to activate the fusion between 2 close surfaces.
# V1.0 Limits : The zone where the density is weak can generate holes when projected on the plane or project unwanted sides of the character. Edges of the character can appear blury or flickery. 
# Further improvements :  V1.0 Need to be tested on denser point clouds (Depth to Color), work on developing a optimized fusion algorithms in the next version.
# V2.0 : Added rasterization to solve density problems and separate the process of perspective fusion in 2 steps (preparation and fusion)
# V2.0 Limits : The perspective projection with triangle rasterization generates now too much data from time to time above all on auto occluded zone by linking two vertices far from eachother
# V2.0 The rasterization might be fastened with a more optimized triangle filling method according to the rasterization rules 
# Parameters : PosColMap sources list, PosColMapToFuse, FinalWidth, FinalHeight, FinalDepth, Bounding Box, Depth fusion distance, Fusion Display, camera, scalar angle limit, voxelize switch (not finished) because it's linked to the export and could not be necessary, damping power, occlude opposite cameras.
# Note : Need edge filter and weighted poscolmaps
# V2.1 Damping method abandonned to the profit of a fixed projection surface attached to the camera => Creation of a virtual kinect
# Compute shader needed : V2.0 PerspectiveFusionTrisDensifierCompute and PerspectiveFusionCompute_prepared
# V2.2 Added the Temporal Anti Aliasing Processing to suppress the edges jittering and be able to turn around the hologram with the camera real time
# Tests : Tested on 5 cams MP4, Double buffer added for MKV and direct live sensors, To be tested on a full 9 cam character
#############################################################################################*/

